      "content": "but \"improving performance\" feels like such a weak cover story. if they have gait and heart rate data, they basically have a biometric signature. i've heard some people online saying the telemetry isn't even being used for the app features, but is being bundled and sold to third-party behavioral analysts. it just seems way too easy to turn fitness data into a way to predict mood or even political leanings. don't you think the technical capability for that kind of profiling is definitely there, even if they officially deny it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
